+++ b/specs/105-sequential-memo-review/runtime.md
@@ -0,0 +1,9 @@
+# Runtime setup and verification
+
+The memo route explicitly uses OpenAI for planning, drafting and auditing. The environment fallback remains available to existing non-memo callers; it cannot silently become the memo writer. Meta reviews the primary draft and any subsequent repaired draft before the final source and substantive gates.
+
+Configure Meta through the existing protected administration integration. The key is encrypted in `management_vault`; activation probes synthetic text only. Existing tested settings now supply the secondary reviewer and preserve the primary writer. Alternatively set server-only `META_KEY` (also accepts `Meta_key`) or `OPENROUTER_API_KEY`, with `META_MODEL` or `OPENROUTER_MODEL`. Paid Meta models still require the existing explicit approval. Never place credentials in source or frontend variables.
+
+`GET /api/health` reports `memoPipeline` with the release revision, primary, secondary and a credential-presence boolean. It does not prove vendor acceptance. An actual memo response reports a completed secondary review only after its response validates. Missing Meta configuration returns `meta_configuration`; primary quota failure returns `billing`, persists `openai_billing`, and is not relabelled source_review. Source failures log fixed issue codes and source counts under the request ID, without facts, prompts or output.
+
+The 2026-11-25 inspected production environment and encrypted store contained no Meta credential. The new key mentioned by the owner was not supplied to or discoverable in this runtime. No revoked conversation key is reused. Provider/account billing cannot be repaired by code or by inventing credentials.
