@@ -0,0 +1,15 @@
+# Sequential memo generation repair
+
+## Scope and observed failures
+The 2026-11-25 synthetic loan test reached source_review (HTTP 422) after 135 seconds. OpenAI returned 429 and the running service silently drafted through Gemini. The procedure panel displayed unknown roles while the extracted form correctly contained the defendant. Meta is absent from the production environment and encrypted provider store; the user's new key must not be inferred or recreated.
+
+## Requirements and acceptance
+- FR-1: Memo planning, drafting and validation use OpenAI explicitly. A rejected OpenAI request must preserve its safe error classification and never silently select Gemini or Meta as writer. Transient rate limits get a bounded retry; quota/auth/model failures do not.
+- FR-2: Meta receives the exact primary drafting input and OpenAI draft, plus approved case data and source context. Its corrected structured content passes the existing citation, facts, role, relief and coverage gates. A failed/unconfigured review is visible and cannot be labelled completed.
+- FR-3: Resolve the secondary credential from server META_KEY/OPENROUTER_API_KEY or the encrypted tested administrator setting. Activating the setting must keep OpenAI primary. Do not log or return keys, prompts or client text.
+- FR-4: Record source rejection codes, source counts and stage under the request ID without case content. Preserve existing screened office drafts against later empty failures. A failed source gate remains pending and must never deliver unverified authorities or consume payment.
+- FR-5: A self-identification containing the client's literal name followed by their role is recognised; opposing-party roles and negated/ambiguous roles cannot overwrite it. The final prepared fields and procedure summary agree.
+- FR-6: Preserve the legal corpus boundary, sources, template, payments, archives and Arabic RTL. No fallback authorities, fictitious citations or disabled source gates.
+
+## Unknowns and live criteria
+The actual OpenAI 429 subtype and the new Meta key's deployment destination are not established. A live success requires both real providers to respond and the synthetic memo to pass the existing legal gates. Unit fixtures establish software behaviour only.
